Loop the OAuth callback server until the real callback arrives.

Upstream calls server.handle_request() exactly once, so any stray request
(browser favicon fetch, Safe Browsing preflight, DNS-over-HTTPS prefetch)
that hits localhost:6600 before Monzo's redirect eats the one request and
the server closes. The subsequent OAuth callback has nowhere to go and
`authorize` exits without exchanging the code for a real user token.

Keep handling requests until we see one whose URL contains `code=`.

--- a/src/pymonzo/utils.py
+++ b/src/pymonzo/utils.py
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@ def get_authorization_response_url(host: str, port: int) -> str:
     """
     wsgi_app = WSGIApp()
     with make_server(host, port, wsgi_app) as server:  # type: ignore
-        server.handle_request()
+        while "code=" not in wsgi_app.last_request_uri:
+            server.handle_request()

     return wsgi_app.last_request_uri
